BOPTools_AlgoTools2D: a new pcurve on a face spanning more than one period
is checked where it is moved to, not twice as far (mitcad#380).

AdjustPCurveOnSurf moves a curve by whole periods of a periodic surface
into the face's parameter range: GeomInt::AdjustPeriodic gives the shift
du from the curve's middle u2 into the range. It was called with u2 as
both the input and the output, so u2 came back already moved; then, on a
face whose range spans more than one period, the classifier checked the
point u2 + du, the curve moved twice, and the shift was corrected from
there (by one period, or since 0510 to the copy inside the face): the
curve itself, moved by du only, ended up that far outside the face.

A threaded hole's cylinders, kept as one face each between helices
running 32 turns, are split into pieces on the one surface by a cross
hole at mid-height; the piece below the hole has a range of 16 periods
lying wholly below the surface's first period. A box cut on that piece
got its section curves (in the first period) moved 16 periods down,
checked 32 periods down, and placed a period above the first one: the
piece's split took them for curves outside it, the cut removed nothing
and its result was invalid.

u2 now keeps the curve's own value, so that the point checked is the one
the curve is moved to. Nothing changes where AdjustPeriodic does not move
the curve, or on faces spanning at most one period, where the check is
not made.

--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKBO/BOPTools/BOPTools_AlgoTools2D.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKBO/BOPTools/BOPTools_AlgoTools2D.cxx
@@ -333,7 +333,10 @@ void BOPTools_AlgoTools2D::AdjustPCurveOnSurf(const BRepAdaptor_Surface&       a
       u2 = UMin + aUPeriod;
     }
     // b. compute du again using clarified value of u2
-    GeomInt::AdjustPeriodic(u2, UMin, UMax, aUPeriod, u2, du, 0.);
+    // u2 stays the curve's own value: the point checked below is u2 + du
+    // (mitcad#380).
+    double aU2Adjusted = u2;
+    GeomInt::AdjustPeriodic(u2, UMin, UMax, aUPeriod, aU2Adjusted, du, 0.);
     //
     if (du == 0.)
     {
